{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7d2888eb5ed3dce9455e1a5c5de750e08ee013018d281166d10d57e34ecdfa1c","digest":{"component_or_area":"fetcher pagination (inbound snapshot)","key_entities":["src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","fetcher._iter_pages","fetcher.collect","_build_snapshot","jira.search.views.default.max","SilentTruncationError","get_parent_map","page_size","startAt","maxResults","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetcher_pagination_heldout.py"],"problem_keywords":["pagination","truncation","silent data loss","inbound snapshot","page advancement","short page handling","offset stall detection"],"propositions":["fetcher._iter_pages terminates on short pages and advances by requested page_size instead of actual page length, causing 92% of issues to be silently lost from the inbound snapshot","Jira Data Center silently truncates maxResults when it exceeds jira.search.views.default.max, which _iter_pages misinterprets as end-of-results instead of a hard cap","The defect affects the shared inbound path used by both Cloud and DC bridges, making this a wider blast radius than adapter-local fixes","A server that ignores startAt can cause _iter_pages to loop forever with repeated pages, requiring an offset-stall guard","The fix must advance by len(page) and terminate only on empty pages, with an offset-stall guard raising SilentTruncationError to prevent infinite loops on unresponsive servers"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787318216474824001,"uuid":"86474eb7-5f1e-4303-9f96-3e44447f73bc"}